# I03.var06 v1.0.1 independent contract gate — GO_CONTRACT_ONLY

Reviewed the frozen, retrospective-only contract draft `i03-var06-v101-retrospective-contract-draft-v5-20261008.json` (216,817 bytes, SHA-256 `66465e9a5df6c3e5a95f6b9b6b046bb6ea3b448a6512cb3e88ff7f2993f803dc`) and its lineage note v4 (5,127 bytes, SHA-256 `cdcb581c84aac705dc79401b8336ac8b010567159e933f86dbf6d56558dbfa2d`). This authorizes **construction of a separate evidence-only package and read-only checker**, not acceptance of the failed v1.0.0 run, a new native call, or publication.

The independent read-only auditor `i03-var06-v101-independent-contract-audit-v5.py` (9,846 bytes, SHA-256 `7456d9adc027f2d6f6e6a33f52e473d795eb3d460e62b575cc99d4b092818525`) exited 0. Its original stdout (459 bytes, SHA-256 `1edd2e848ec98c9f0c9e2514903154ce465a2f034a879d66285ec3665ac22d14`) reports 214 accepted source disk/Git byte pairs via Git blob OIDs, 118 mandatory accepted raw/context files, the frozen 445-record v100 manifest, 31 additional v100 source and 31 review files, all 26 failed-run files, the 23-file closure and 25-file failure seal, and 20 additional original case/root transport and guard files. Stderr was empty. The auditor also checked installed/documentation pins, the exact historical 491-entry catalog archive against the current typed append-only prefix and metadata, and exhaustive six-table/5,210-cell field-class partitions. The v4 auditor was retained separately before the v5 custody revision.

The contract consumes the **unchanged** failed native log: one OUT task starts at h6 with printed transfer time 4 and its linked arrival is at h10. It requires a derived quantity ledger with one local P-CREW leaving at h6, one task quantity in transfer during [6,10), then one completed OUT task quantity. These quantities do not identify a persistent person or establish an independently observed outside resource pool. The accepted TFDT0 comparator has printed 0 and arrival at h6. Every log line, continuation, task identity, route, quantity, ordering and terminal edge must be reconciled directly from original raw bytes.

Each arm must independently reconcile its complete report schema and 5,210 expected cells from source, typed events, and predeclared presentation rules. The one observed PDESC difference and 5,209 other matching cells are only a cross-check. The five ResourceResultsTotal binary32 means are exact. Unexplained cells or a widened tolerance mean NO_GO. Source/export TFDT4 and all roundtrip metadata remain mandatory. The original behavior checker exit 1 and `passed:false` remain part of the evidence; its separate independent replay `KeyError: 'owned_exact_archive'` occurred before physical parsing and must not be represented as an observed physical verdict.

The original v100 prospective claim remains **NO_GO_RUN**. The manual's OUT TFDT description is not rewritten into a universal rule; this contract tests a bounded counterexample for the installed build and fixed row. No claim is made for IN/BETWEEN, other OUT rows, person identity, or a general transport algorithm. Original accepted raw paths and the failed v100 run paths remain mandatory and fail closed if unavailable. Inert byte-identical copies are planned only for unpublished non-run history and small context; original and copied identities stay distinct. A later checker and publication require independent exact-file gates.
